---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="About FilamentPath: independent, data-driven reviews of FDM 3D printing equipment. Who runs it and how it's funded."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'About', url: '/about/' },
  ]}
  showByline={false}
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <h1 id="about">About</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      FilamentPath helps readers choose better 3D printing equipment by
      comparing real specifications, prices, and use cases across FDM
      printers, filaments, and accessories. Less hype, more numbers.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      An independent reviews and comparison site for FDM (fused
      deposition modeling) 3D printing equipment. Every product page is
      built from verifiable specifications, not generic opinion. The
      question we try to answer is straightforward:
      <em>which printer (or filament, or accessory) fits your specific
      use case at your specific budget?</em>
    </p>

    <h2>How we make money</h2>
    <p>
      We earn affiliate commission when readers buy through product
      links. As an Amazon Associate, we earn from qualifying purchases.
      Affiliate revenue funds the site and keeps it free of paid
      advertising. We do not accept payment from manufacturers in
      exchange for coverage, and we do not accept free units in
      exchange for rankings.
    </p>

    <h2 id="disclosure">Affiliate disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      Many product links on FilamentPath are affiliate links. If you
      click such a link and make a qualifying purchase, we may earn a
      small commission at no additional cost to you. As an Amazon
      Associate, we earn from qualifying purchases. Where direct
      manufacturer programs apply (e.g. Bambu Lab, Creality, Anycubic),
      we disclose them on each affected page.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
    <p>
      Our recommendations are anchored in three things:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Verifiable specifications.</strong> Build volume, layer
        height range, max bed and nozzle temperature, compatible
        materials, hotend design, auto-leveling system, footprint &mdash;
        publicly documented attributes we can compare side by side.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Use-case fit.</strong> The "best" printer depends on
        whether you're printing PLA minis, functional PETG parts, or
        flexible TPU; whether you need an enclosure for ABS; whether
        you'll print one part a week or run a small farm. Content is
        organised around those decisions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Price tier transparency.</strong> Products are bucketed
        by price (budget, mid, premium, pro). Comparisons happen within
        tiers; we don't pretend a $250 printer competes with a $700 one
        &mdash; though we will tell you when the difference doesn't
        matter for your use case.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't post fake reviews.</li>
      <li>We don't accept payment in exchange for ranking position.</li>
      <li>We don't recommend products outside the budget you indicated.</li>
      <li>We don't simulate hands-on testing for products we haven't actually used; comparative analysis is clearly labeled as such.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who runs it</h2>
    <p>
      FilamentPath is run by a single editor &mdash; a Colombian data
      scientist relocated abroad &mdash; who runs an FDM 3D printer at
      home as a maker hobbyist. The data-science background informs how
      product pages are structured: structured specs, documented
      methodology, and a clear separation between what we know
      (verifiable facts) and what we infer (aggregate user reports).
    </p>

    <h2>FDM-first, resin later</h2>
    <p>
      Initial coverage focuses on FDM (filament) printers, filaments,
      and FDM accessories. Resin (SLA / MSLA) coverage will open later
      and will include explicit safety and ventilation guidance &mdash;
      uncured resin is irritant and the workflow differs from FDM in
      important ways.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@filamentpath.com">hello@filamentpath.com</a>.
      <em>(Email forwarding will be configured shortly after launch.)</em>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 2rem auto 4rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .legal-page h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-page .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: #444;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .legal-page h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-page ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .legal-page li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
